<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    {% comment %}
      Design tokens, generated from packages/tokens/src/tokens.ts — the same
      source that produces the Tailwind theme for apps/web and apps/mobile.
      Loaded before everything else so merchant settings in 'css-variables'
      and any section styles can override individual values.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{ 'tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}

    {% # Inlined CSS Variables %}
    {% render 'css-variables' %}

    {% comment %}
      DM Sans and DM Mono (SHO-110): the same files apps/web serves, synced
      from packages/tokens by `pnpm --filter @formulate/theme build`. The body
      weight is preloaded because it paints most of the page; the other
      weights load on demand through @font-face.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{ 'fonts.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {{ 'dm-sans-latin-400-normal.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}

    {% # Load and preload the critical CSS %}
    {{ 'critical.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}

    {% # Social, title, etc. %}
    {% render 'meta-tags' %}

    {% # Import map and web components %}
    {% render 'scripts' %}

    {{ content_for_header }}
  </head>

  <body>
    {% comment %}
      First thing on the page, so one Tab reaches it and Enter skips the header
      and its collection links (WCAG 2.4.1, SHO-152). Hidden until focused.
    {% endcomment %}
    <a class="skip-link" href="#MainContent">{{ 'general.skip_to_content' | t }}</a>

    {% sections 'header-group' %}

    {% comment %}
      The page's main landmark, which the theme didn't have. tabindex="-1" so
      the skip link moves focus here, not only the scroll position.
    {% endcomment %}
    <main id="MainContent" tabindex="-1">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    {% sections 'footer-group' %}

    {% comment %}
      The cart drawer lives in the layout so it is present on every page — a
      shopper can add from a product page and see the drawer without a
      navigation.

      The <dialog> is here rather than inside the section on purpose. Cart
      mutations re-render the section and swap its contents in, and the dialog
      surviving that swap is what preserves its open state, its place in the
      top layer, and any transition mid-flight. Re-rendering the dialog itself
      would close the drawer on every quantity change.
    {% endcomment %}
    <cart-drawer>
      <dialog class="cart-drawer" aria-label="{{ 'cart.title' | t }}">
        {% section 'cart-drawer' %}
      </dialog>
    </cart-drawer>
  </body>
</html>
